OL,3,GNEWSAHow the hair of a museum bear is
OL,4,Ahelping tackle wildlife crime
OL,5,
OL,6,FA student has been using hair from a
OL,7,F120-year-old museum exhibit to help
OL,8,Ffind new ways of solving wildlife
OL,9,Fcrime.
OL,11,FThe taxidermy bear, known as Boris, is
OL,12,Fa popular feature at the Museum of
OL,13,FChelmsford and is regarded as its
OL,14,Funofficial mascot.
OL,16,FHayden Leigh, a forensic science
OL,17,Fgraduate at the University of
OL,18,FStaffordshire, is using samples taken
OL,19,Ffrom his hair to help protect
OL,20,Fmodern-day brown bears from illegal
OL,21,Fpoaching.
OL,23,APub: 06-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
